From a1ed6102076425c1679f5a164f53757a5f5a6533 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 17:35:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 514/913] core: notif: fix assert if atomic_cb is null

Atomic callback is not mandatory. And then ndrv->atomic_cb will be null
and is_unpaged will always return false.

Do "is_unpaged" check only is ndrv->atomic_cb is not null.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git a57132d81414f2caf574f39d0a107c243ea4c8d3 core: notif: fix assert if atomic_cb is null]
Signed-off-by: Valentin Caron <valentin.caron@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Ib5f07561ef14411b58862a76a221dbf38a0a0d65
---
 core/kernel/notif.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/kernel/notif.c b/core/kernel/notif.c
index fa879e11d..5a3f15a89 100644
--- a/core/kernel/notif.c
+++ b/core/kernel/notif.c
@@ -60,7 +60,8 @@ void notif_register_driver(struct notif_driver *ndrv)
 {
 	uint32_t old_itr_status = 0;
 
-	assert(is_nexus(ndrv) && is_unpaged(ndrv->atomic_cb));
+	assert(is_nexus(ndrv));
+	assert(ndrv->atomic_cb ? is_unpaged(ndrv->atomic_cb) : true);
 
 	old_itr_status = cpu_spin_lock_xsave(&notif_lock);
 
-- 
